==English==
[[Image:Apple rotting on the tree - geograph.org.uk - 5512352.jpg|The apple on the right shows signs of '''decay'''.|thumb]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱh₂d-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|decaien||to decrease, diminish}} and {{m|enm|decai||deterioration, decline in value}}, from {{der|en|xno|decheoir|decaeir|t=to fall away, decay, decline}}, from {{der|en|la-vul||*dēcadere}}, etymologically restored form of {{der|en|la|dēcidō|dēcidere|t=to fall down, to fail, sink or perish}}, from {{m|la|de-||of, from, away, down}} + {{m|la|cadō|cadere|t=to fall}}. Compare {{m|en|decadent}} and {{m|en|decadence}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈkeɪ/|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪ|s=2}}
* {{enPR|dē-kāʹ|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/diˈkeɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-decay.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|de|cay}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} [[rot|Rot]]; any [[process]]es or [[result]] of organic matter being gradually [[decompose]]d, especially by microbial action.
#: {{ux|en|tooth '''decay'''/dental '''decay'''&mdash;wood-'''decay''' fungi&mdash;bacterial '''decay'''&mdash;photochemical '''decay'''}}
#* {{RQ:Wells Time Machine|chapter=X|passage=I fancied at first the stuff was paraffin wax, and smashed the jar accordingly. But the odor of camphor was unmistakable. It struck me as singularly odd, that among the universal '''decay''', this volatile substance had chanced to survive, perhaps through many thousand years.}}
# {{1|deterioration}} of [[condition]]; loss of [[status]], [[quality]], [[strength]], or [[fortune]].
#: {{ux|en|civic and moral '''decay'''&mdash;systemic '''decay'''&mdash;fall into '''decay'''&mdash;urban '''decay'''&mdash;arrested '''decay'''&mdash;memory '''decay'''}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Barnaby Rudge|10|passage=Although the best room of the inn, it had the melancholy aspect of grandeur in '''decay''', and was much too vast for comfort.}}
# {{lb|en|physics}} {{1|radioactive decay}}; decomposition of an atom or its nucleus.
#: {{syn|en|[[nuclear decay|nuclear '''decay''']]&mdash;[[atomic decay|atomic '''decay''']]}}
#: {{ux|en|alpha '''decay'''&mdash;gamma '''decay'''&mdash;fission '''decay'''&mdash;'''decay''' chain}}
# {{lb|en|physics}} {{1|particle decay}}; decomposition of a [[sub-atomic]] particle.
# Continuous decrease of a quantity.
#: {{ux|en|exponential '''decay'''&mdash;'''decay''' rate&mdash;orbital '''decay'''&mdash;'''decay''' time&mdash;'''decay''' constant&mdash;time '''decay'''}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[overthrow|Overthrow]], [[destruction]], [[ruin]], [[death]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=vi|page=40|passage=Let’s cheere our ſouldiers to incounter him,<br>That grieuous image of ingratitude:<br>That fiery thirſter after Soueraigntie: {{...}}<br>Reſolue my Lords and louing ſouldiers now,<br>To ſaue your king and country from '''decay''':}}
# {{lb|en|programming}} {{1|array decay}}.

====Usage notes====
* Historically, definition 1 could not include our modern theories of how such ''rot'' occurs. It was something that was restricted to animal and vegetable matter.

